Your letter 028, taken: 10 pt, the 9 pt floor and the margins stay; the folio alone stays.

Hyphenation: book.css already asks for it (hyphens: auto, and the book's language is en-GB), but the container's Chromium has no hyphenation dictionaries: I printed a test with long words in en-GB, en-US and en, and it broke none of them. No hyphenation library is installed either, and I will not download one. So the justified body keeps its gaps in our PDF. Leanpub's PDF is its own engine and may hyphenate.

The alternative that works here: ragged right (text-align: left) for the body, which opens no gaps at all. I have changed nothing; say if you want it.

